    "research_summary": "His research develops machine-learning-based control charts for monitoring and detecting anomalies in non-Gaussian and multivariate processes, including Poisson, Gamma, and binomial data. He integrates classical control-chart theory (Shewhart, EWMA, and CUSUM) with predictive models and evaluates detection performance through Monte Carlo simulation, covering run-length behaviour, false-alarm rates, and robustness under distributional shifts. He also contributed to a semi-parametric Bayesian physics-informed neural network framework for uncertainty-aware prediction in dynamical systems.",
